---
const siteTitle = "Baseline preferences – La Familia";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{siteTitle}</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        --text: #1f2933;
        --muted: #5b6570;
        --border: #d7dce1;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --accent: #2f5d7c;
        --background: #f6f7f9;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: "Inter", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background: var(--background);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 960px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 64px 24px 104px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 32px;
      }

      h1,
      h2 {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      p {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .section {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 28px 32px;
      }

      .subtitle {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        max-width: 720px;
      }

      .note {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="section">
        <h1>Baseline travel preferences</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          This reference captures the general criteria we use to assess destinations, routing, and
          trip structure. It is stable across themes unless explicitly overridden by a theme page.
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          These preferences reflect how we travel as a family and are intended to stay consistent
          across multiple trip ideas.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What we like</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Walkable areas with clear logistics and dependable local transit.</li>
          <li>Balanced itineraries that preserve recovery time and unplanned evenings.</li>
          <li>Cultural depth, local food access, and calm nights over high-energy scenes.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What we avoid</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Frequent hotel changes or multi-leg transfers that add fatigue.</li>
          <li>Overly dense schedules that remove downtime or increase rushing.</li>
          <li>Noise-heavy environments that affect sleep or focus.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What we look for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A stable base with options for short day trips.</li>
          <li>Weather and seasonality that align with planned activities.</li>
          <li>Costs that fit a mid-range family budget with predictable expenses.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Logistics style</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Prefer direct flights or single-stop routing with reasonable layovers.</li>
          <li>Prioritize ground transport that is legible, safe, and low-friction.</li>
          <li>Accommodations should include shared space for quiet breaks.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Safety and calm vibe</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Health access and safety fundamentals are non-negotiable.</li>
          <li>We favor locations that feel calm, predictable, and suitable for rest.</li>
          <li>Evening pacing should support early nights and low-noise environments.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
